# {{.Name}}

Go backend (Chi + {{.Dialect}}) scaffolded by **goforge** following the MogRex Backend Engineering Standard.

## Quick start

```bash
# .env was created for you — adjust DATABASE_URL, then:
make migrate-up     # apply migrations
make run            # start the server on :8080
```

## Layout

```
cmd/server/main.go        entry point
cmd/migrate/main.go       migration runner (golang-migrate)
internal/config           typed env configuration (+ .env loader)
internal/database         connection pool
internal/domain           entities, DTOs, repository/service interfaces, sentinel errors
internal/handlers         HTTP handlers, router, response envelopes
internal/services         business logic
internal/repositories     SQL + in-memory repositories
internal/middleware       request id, logger, generated middleware
internal/app              generated wiring (modules_gen.go, middleware_gen.go)
migrations/               versioned SQL migrations
forge.yaml                schema: project settings + modules
```

## Working with goforge

```bash
goforge generate module order     # add a module (prompts for fields) and generate it
goforge generate middleware auth  # add a middleware
goforge sync                      # re-read forge.yaml and regenerate
goforge migrate up|down|status    # run migrations
goforge doctor                    # gofmt + build + vet + test (+ lint)
```

Files carrying `Code generated by goforge. DO NOT EDIT.` are rewritten on every sync.
Every other generated file is yours to edit: goforge records a hash of what it wrote
(`.forge/manifest.json`, commit it) and will not overwrite a file you changed unless you pass `--force`.

## Migrations

```bash
make migrate-up
make migrate-down n=1
make migrate-status
make migrate-create name=add_status_to_orders
make migrate-force version=<version>   # after a failed (dirty) migration
```

